A resolve larger than its texture is shrunk only for a scaled scene (both directions, a texture of 64x64 or more); the
Xenos resolves 8x8 blocks and copies what fits, and GTA IV's 8x8 resolves into its 8x1 luminance were averaged to 0.

--- a/src/x360/deko/destinos.cpp
+++ b/src/x360/deko/destinos.cpp
@@ -1446,8 +1446,12 @@
       const uint32_t alto = std::min(pedido_alto, cabe_alto);
       // A scene larger than its resolved texture (an internal resolution above the front buffer's) is shrunk with
       // a linear blit, as the Vulkan path does; otherwise it is copied texel for texel.
-      const bool encoger = cabe_ancho && cabe_alto &&
-                           (pedido_ancho * 4 >= cabe_ancho * 5 || pedido_alto * 4 >= cabe_alto * 5);
+      // Only a scaled scene: larger in both directions and into a texture of some size. The Xenos resolves in 8x8
+      // blocks and copies what fits: GTA IV resolves an 8x8 rectangle into its 8x1 luminance textures (and 8x8 into
+      // 8x5), and the shrink averaged row 0, its only value, with the 7 empty rows below: the adapted luminance came
+      // out 0 and the tonemap burned the frame white outdoors and black indoors.
+      const bool encoger = cabe_ancho >= 64 && cabe_alto >= 64 && pedido_ancho * 4 >= cabe_ancho * 5 &&
+                           pedido_alto * 4 >= cabe_alto * 5;
       // nfsmw_nativo_frontal_perezoso: the whole scene to the front buffer of the last Swap, not read back.
       const int32_t maximo_lectura = REXCVAR_GET(nfsmw_nativo_leer_resueltas_texels);
       const bool se_lee = maximo_lectura > 0 && uint64_t(ancho) * alto <= uint64_t(maximo_lectura);
